{
  "_meta": {
    "name": "trading_rules",
    "version": "2.2",
    "effective_date": "[REDACTED]03",
    "changelog": "v2.2 ([REDACTED]): added capit_margin_lever block ([REDACTED], enabled=false) — margin on the CAPIT bear-washout sleeve only, fixed f=1.3, gate dd52<=-20%, DNSE [REDACTED] package 1840, [REDACTED] only. Wiring + rehearsal complete (job Taylor_20260803_122554, report mike/agents/Taylor/research/margin_kelly_production_wiring_20260803.md); ZERO live behaviour change while enabled=false. Scope is exactly what the p1-p5 research chain verified (p5 engine tier, quant-skeptic [REDACTED]D-medium: dCAGR +0.663pp, dMaxDD worse 0.067pp, DSR 1.0, PBO 0.10-0.14) — NOT the p4 proxy numbers (+1.82pp), which p5 showed inflate both directions. Flipping enabled=true requires a separate explicit user confirmation; no agent may flip it. | v2.1 ([REDACTED]03): added neutral_parking section (governance policy, not a research change) — codifies the engine default that at DT5G NEUTRAL with 0 active BAL/LAG deals, idle cash parks into [REDACTED]V at 70% OF THE IDLE POOL (not a total-equity cap). Reason: go-live [REDACTED] DollarBill wrote target_equity_pct=93.8% straight into a trade plan JSON that passed no policy/backtest gate; user caught it via direct questioning; backtest confirmed 70% is the risk-adjusted optimum. Evidence pinned: jobs Taylor_20260703_113818 (70 vs 94 isolated, quant-skeptic [REDACTED]11:57:15), _120555 (70-100 sweep, no inflection), _130720 (CANONICAL full 2-book NAV: park0.70 CAGR26.83/Sh1.78/DD-16.5/Cal1.63 DOMINATES park0.94 28.01/1.66/-18.8/1.49 and park1.00 29.30/1.65/-19.3/1.52 on Sharpe+Calmar+MaxDD every window), _153738 (70 = properly-tested level, not a taste floor). Added risk_dial_override (PROPOSED/[REDACTED], same guardrail pattern as deep_cheap_recovery_override/v25_leverage): any plan setting NEUTRAL park!=0.70 must carry risk_dial_confirmed_by_user:true + risk_dial_warning_acknowledged citing the job-130720 Sharpe/Calmar/DD cost, else Mafee BLOCKS. No algorithm/backtest logic changed — policy record only. | v2.0 ([REDACTED]29): added gap_adaptive_fill block (PROPOSED, enabled=false) — Layer-3 fill timing becomes gap_z-conditional: abnormal DOWN-gap (gap_z<-2) on a buy-list name -> BUY-AT-OPEN (current rule wrongly waits to 11:15, leaving ~173-206 bps); UP-gap unchanged. Evidence gap_adaptive_proxy.py (daily N=408k IS+OOS) + gap_path_crosscheck.py (16-name 1-min). Pure execution, zero alpha risk; paper-first, LIVE needs user approval. | v1.9 ([REDACTED]27): added v25_leverage block — NAMING V2.5 = V2.4 + leverage (user); account [REDACTED] (DNSE [REDACTED] loan_package_id=1840, borrow 12.5%) user-confirmed; documents B2(breaker-15% DONE)/B3(NAV-cap100B DONE)/B4(PE-freshness DONE) safety gates + risk layering. STATUS=[REDACTED] (prep) — paper until live-recommend integration + final user go-ahead; go-live [REDACTED]30 = V2.4 leverage-free, unaffected. v1.8 ([REDACTED]27): MGE ceiling RAISED 1.30 -> 1.50 per Spyros mge20-tail-review decision (mge20-tail-review-REJECT-cap-at-1.5, [REDACTED]27) — Taylor full 4-point MGE sweep on stable cache showed 1.5 better in-sample (lean default) over 1.3, LUMPY but manageable; 2.0 rejected (tail risk). Episode-drawdown breaker threshold updated -12% -> -15% to match the wider 1.5x ceiling (Spyros: -12% was calibrated for 1.3x; at 1.5x the wider position warrants 3pp more tolerance before knife-catcher fires). Spyros implements in risk_monitor.py (S4 breach = BOT_STOP + Telegram + halt-review flag for first 6m go-live). v1.7 ([REDACTED]26): added macro_kill_switches section (3 RECOVERY_PARK suspend conditions required by Spyros's v24-golive-risk-review sign-off, [REDACTED]23) ahead of go-live [REDACTED]30 — (A) SBV deposit rate >7.5% -> suspend new recovery deploy (outer hard-stop on top of the money_condition throttle); (B) median liquid-universe pb_z > -0.3 while a recovery episode is active -> tighten (stop adding, market no longer cheap; -0.5-in/-0.3-out hysteresis vs deep_cheap_recovery_override episode-open); (C) cumulative intra-episode NAV drawdown > -12% from episode entry -> HALT via BOT_STOP (knife-catching circuit breaker, distinct from the intraday -5% brake). All are SUSPEND (auto-arming, not permanent-off) except (C) which needs human review to restart. v1.6 ([REDACTED]23): deep_cheap_recovery_override ceiling TIGHTENED 1.50 -> 1.30. v1.5 ([REDACTED]23): money_condition dep_floor 0.06->0.075. v1.4 ([REDACTED]22): added money_condition.",
    "author": "Taylor (quant/algo)",
    "owners": "Taylor owns this file (single source of truth for risk/sizing limits)",
    "consumers": {
      "DollarBill": "reads to build data/plan_<acct>_<T+1>.json (sizing within these limits)",
      "Mafee": "hard-blocks any order/plan beyond these limits (2nd gate after the approved plan)",
      "Spyros": "owns BOT_STOP kill-switch; enforces the daily-loss circuit breaker threshold set here"
    },
    "approval": {
      "applies_to": "live",
      "approved_by": "user",
      "approved_date": "[REDACTED]26",
      "live_effective": "[REDACTED]",
      "live_requires_user_approval": true,
      "note": "User approved live on [REDACTED]26 for go-live [REDACTED]. Mafee must refuse live execution until today >= live_effective AND [REDACTED] account enabled=true in trading_bot_accounts.json."
    },
    "units": {
      "scheme": "NAV-relative",
      "nav_source": "Mafee reads live NAV from the latest data/eod_account_<date>.json (Mafee EOD snapshot); all *_pct limits multiply that NAV. No capital is hardcoded so the limits auto-scale on deposit/withdrawal.",
      "pct_convention": "fractions (0.10 = 10%); loss limits negative (-0.05 = -5%)"
    },
    "consistency_with_bot_config": {
      "file": "secrets/trading_bot_config.json (Mafee-owned execution mechanics)",
      "rule": "where keys overlap, THIS file is the authoritative POLICY; trading_bot_config.json must stay consistent.",
      "mapping": {
[REDACTED]"participation_cap -> max_participation": "0.10 == bot 0.10 (match)",
[REDACTED]"plan_deviation_tolerance_pct -> qty_tolerance_pct": "0.05 == bot 0.05 (match)",
[REDACTED]"max_orders_per_day -> max_orders_per_day": "60 == bot 60 (match)",
[REDACTED]"min_order_value_vnd -> min_order_value": "5,000,000 == bot 5M (match)",
[REDACTED]"max_value_per_order_pct": "NAV-relative parent cap; bot max_child_value 200M slices within it",
[REDACTED]"max_daily_gross_pct": "0.40*NAV ~= bot max_daily_gross_value 20B at 50B NAV"
      }
    }
  },
  "sizing": {
    "gate_rating_max": 3,
    "gate_rating_note": "only 8L as-of rating <=3 eligible (fa_ratings_8l). Validated robust-optimal [REDACTED]22: 4 candidate enhancements all failed OOS/cosmetic, simple yieldcombo gate stands.",
    "[REDACTED]_pct": 0.1,
    "[REDACTED]_note": "max 10% of NAV per single ticker (V2.4 namecap). Concentration ceiling DollarBill sizes within.",
    "min_order_value_vnd": 5000000
  },
  "neutral_parking": {
    "_principle": "When DT5G state == NEUTRAL and the two core books (BAL momentum + LAG PEAD) have NO deal meeting their entry standard at that moment, the IDLE portion of NAV is parked into the [REDACTED]V yieldcombo sleeve at a FIXED 70% of that idle pool. This 70% is a fraction of the IDLE POOL (idle_pool = NAV - active_BAL_LAG_stock_value), NOT a cap on total portfolio equity: when BAL/LAG DO hold real deals, total stock exposure can run far above 70% of NAV (by design — this rule does not apply then, it governs only what to do with the leftover cash). The rule exists to close the go-live gap where a target equity % was written straight into a trade plan without passing any policy/backtest gate (see _meta changelog v2.1).",
    "default_park_of_idle_pct": 0.7,
    "default_park_note": "PARK 70% of idle cash into [REDACTED]V (30 names, [REDACTED] 0.10, gate rating<=3, yieldcombo 1/PE+1/PCF). This is the engine default — the risk-adjusted optimum, NOT a discretionary floor.",
    "evidence": {
      "Taylor_20260703_113818": "70% vs 94% at NEUTRAL / 0-active-pick, isolated sleeve. quant-skeptic [REDACTED](verify [REDACTED]03T11:57:15): pushing 94% buys ZERO risk-adjusted edge over 70%.",
      "Taylor_20260703_120555": "exposure sweep 70-100%: 94% is NOT a special ceiling — the whole band is Sharpe-neutral with no inflection point in the isolated measure; V2.5 lever does NOT stack onto this (disjoint regimes).",
      "Taylor_20260703_130720": "CANONICAL numbers, full 2-book NAV compounding (BAL+LAG [REDACTED]-on + [REDACTED]V parking idle cash), 2014->[REDACTED]19 @50B, DT5G, threads=1, self-check 0 VND. PINNED to data/results_registry.md.",
      "Taylor_20260703_153738": "confirms 70% is the properly-tested/approved level, NOT a 'flexible floor to taste'."
    },
    "measured_tradeoff_job_130720": {
      "note": "FULL 2-book NAV, full window. 94% and 100% buy raw nominal CAGR but LOSE Sharpe + Calmar + MaxDD in EVERY window (IS and OOS). 70% DOMINATES all risk-adjusted metrics.",
      "park_0.70": { "CAGR": 0.2683, "Sharpe": 1.78, "MaxDD": -0.165, "Calmar": 1.63 },
      "park_0.94": { "CAGR": 0.2801, "Sharpe": 1.66, "MaxDD": -0.188, "Calmar": 1.49 },
      "park_1.00": { "CAGR": 0.2930, "Sharpe": 1.65, "MaxDD": -0.193, "Calmar": 1.52 },
      "verdict": "70 risk-adj optimal; production 3:0.70 (NEUTRAL state=3, park=0.70) correct. Higher park = pay Sharpe/Calmar/DD for nominal CAGR only."
    },
    "status": "ACTIVE — engine default 0.70 is the enforced rule. Any deviation requires the risk_dial_override below.",
    "risk_dial_override": {
      "_principle": "The user MAY deliberately choose a higher NEUTRAL park level (e.g. 0.80 / 0.90 / 0.94 / 1.00) to accept WORSE risk-adjusted performance in exchange for higher nominal CAGR. This is a legitimate risk-appetite dial — but it must be a CONSCIOUS, logged choice, never a silent default that slips into a plan. Same guardrail pattern as deep_cheap_recovery_override / v25_leverage: OFF until an explicit, evidence-acknowledged user confirmation is present in the plan.",
      "status": "PROPOSED/[REDACTED] no override active. Engine uses 0.70 until a plan carries the two confirmation fields below.",
      "rule": "Any trade plan that sets NEUTRAL parking != 0.70 (of idle pool) MUST carry BOTH fields: (1) risk_dial_confirmed_by_user: true; (2) risk_dial_warning_acknowledged citing the exact cost from measured_tradeoff_job_130720 (Sharpe 1.78->lower, Calmar 1.63->lower, MaxDD -16.5%->deeper). If EITHER field is missing, Mafee (2nd gate) MUST BLOCK the plan.",
      "required_fields": {
[REDACTED]"risk_dial_confirmed_by_user": "boolean — must be literally true; a plan proposing park!=0.70 without it is blocked.",
[REDACTED]"risk_dial_warning_acknowledged": "string/object — must quote the risk-adjusted cost table from measured_tradeoff_job_130720 (Sharpe/Calmar/MaxDD at the chosen park level vs 0.70). A generic acknowledgement without the actual numbers does NOT satisfy the gate."
      },
      "enforcement": "DollarBill must not set park!=0.70 without user instruction + both fields. Mafee hard-blocks any plan with NEUTRAL parking != 0.70 lacking either field (same mechanical block as an over-limit order). Changing the engine DEFAULT away from 0.70 requires user approval applied to LIVE (owners rule)."
    }
  },
  "execution_limits": {
    "max_value_per_order_pct": 0.05,
    "max_value_per_order_note": "single parent order <= 5% NAV; bot slices into <=200M children",
    "participation_cap": 0.1,
    "participation_cap_note": "buy/sell <= 10% of the ticker's cumulative matched volume that day",
    "max_orders_per_day": 60,
    "max_daily_gross_pct": 0.4,
    "max_daily_gross_note": "total day turnover (buy+sell GTGD) <= 40% NAV",
    "max_[REDACTED]re_pct": 1.5,
    "max_[REDACTED]re_note": "DEFAULT hard ceiling on gross book exposure = 150% NAV = max 50% borrowed. RAISED 1.30 -> 1.50 ([REDACTED]27) per mge20-tail-review (Spyros). Mafee blocks any plan above this UNLESS the deep_cheap_recovery_override below is active.",
    "deep_cheap_recovery_override": {
      "max_[REDACTED]re_pct": 1.5,
      "max_[REDACTED]re_ceiling_note": "RAISED 1.30 -> 1.50 ([REDACTED]27) per Spyros mge20-tail-review: Taylor full 4-point MGE sweep on stable cache showed 1.5 better in-sample (lean default), 2.0 REJECTED (tail risk at Q1_s4_fire). Episode-drawdown breaker recalibrated to -15% at 1.5x ceiling (was -12% for 1.3x). Previous: TIGHTENED 1.50 -> 1.30 ([REDACTED]23) based on pt_v23 real-margin with depth=ON; [REDACTED]27 sweep runs Config-D with depth=OFF which changes tail profile. Ceiling 2.0 remains REJECTED.",
      "condition": "ALL THREE: (1) DT5G state in {CRISIS, BEAR}; (2) median liquid-universe pb_z <= -0.7 (GENUINELY cheap vs own 5Y history — NOT cheap-vs-recent-peak; falling-knife filter: REJECTED Jun-2022 pb_z +0.75 despite -25% from top, FIRED at COVID-2020 pb_z -0.78); (3) money_condition below — system deposit rate LOW enough that cash opportunity-cost does not beat deploying.",
      "money_condition": {
[REDACTED]"rule": "scale the recovery deploy / >1.0x leverage budget by m = clip((dep_ceiling - deposit_rate)/(dep_ceiling - dep_floor), 0, 1); dep_floor=0.075, dep_ceiling=0.12. Deploy/lever fully only when deposit<=7.5%; ZERO extra deploy when deposit>=12% (hold cash even if pb_z cheap). Linear throttle between.",
[REDACTED]"why": "2011-extension backtest (backtest_recovery_alloc_2011.py, [REDACTED]22): deploying into the 2012 deep-cheap crisis LOST to baseline because deposit was 14% (cash earned 14% risk-free) + the recovery was L-shaped/slow. The deposit-gate restored 2011-13 to baseline (+8.4%), kept the 2020 win, gave best full-period CAGR 12.8%/Sharpe 1.11/Calmar 0.68. Encodes 'cautious when macro bad' + 'cheapness vs deposit rate' using the RELIABLE deposit series (pre-2014 PE is corrupt -> a 1/PE Fed-gate is unusable).",
[REDACTED]"floor_calibration": "dep_floor=0.075 (DORMANT) chosen over 0.06 (ACTIVE) after measuring both in pt_v23 ([REDACTED]23): floor=0.075 -> avg m=1.00 -> CAGR 31.81% BYTE-IDENTICAL to baseline (gate never bit, deposit <=7.5% all of 2014-26). floor=0.06 -> avg m=0.85 -> 30.83% (-0.98pp, worse Sharpe/MaxDD/Calmar) because it wrongly trimmed the 2022 SCB-hike deploy which then recovered strongly in 2023. floor=0.075 distinguishes a TRUE high-rate crisis (>7.5%, 2012-like) from a moderate defensive hike. Consistent with the post-2011 disciplined-SBV macro-view.",
[REDACTED]"dormancy": "deposit has been <=7.5% throughout 2014-2026 -> at floor=0.075 this gate is DORMANT in the DT5G era (m=1, ZERO change to the pinned recovery-park 31.81%, self-check 0 VND). It is FORWARD INSURANCE that only arms if rates spike >7.5% in a future crisis. Same fail-safe-not-return-enhancer profile as DT5G itself.",
[REDACTED]"source": "deposit_rate_vn.DEPOSIT_EVENTS (Big-4 12M term, causal/announced); Mafee/Winston confirm the live deposit figure feeding any LIVE use."
      },
      "scaling": "DEPTH-SCALED on pb_z AND money-gated: leverage rises with cheapness toward the 1.50 ceiling at the deepest cheap, THEN multiplied by money_condition m; base (no margin) otherwise. Bet bigger the cheaper — but only when cash is also cheap, and never above 1.50x (revised ceiling from mge20-tail-review).",
      "safety_basis": "TWO limits bind, take the tighter: (1) margin-call buffer — verified call at -44% market drop @1.5x (Mafee broker-API + Wendy), DNSE nets account-level; (2) EPISODE-DD BREAKER — S4 at -15% from episode-entry NAV (Spyros risk_monitor.py) fires BEFORE margin call. At 1.5x ceiling, Config-D (depth=OFF) tail is acceptable; 2.0x rejected at mge20-tail-review. 2.0x long-rejected (call buffer ~1.2x).",
      "evidence_caveat": "the >1.0x margin portion has fired only ONCE in 2014-2026 (COVID 2020) -> deploy DELIBERATELY as opportunistic; core stays 1.0x full-beta. Limit is EVIDENCE (n=1), not call-risk.",
      "status": "PROPOSED (user-agreed concept [REDACTED]22) — paper until user go-live approval + Spyros risk review. Also confirm DNSE force-sell account-netting with Mafee.",
      "strategic_note": "user thesis + Taylor IC (value-edge=0 at EXBULL, +0.148 in DOWN): the leverage budget belongs in deep-cheap RECOVERY, not EXBULL euphoria. Future: consider TIGHTENING EXBULL below 1.30 and shifting that budget to recovery (DT5G allocation-curve change, separate from this cap)."
    },
    "sector_cap": "DELIBERATELY NONE (user [REDACTED]22): VN investable quality is structurally concentrated (banks/securities/real-estate/some retail/few strong manufacturers); a sector cap would force dilution away from the strong names and HURT performance. V2.4 uses [REDACTED] (10%) only, NOT sector_cap. Do not add."
  },
  "risk_circuit_breakers": {
    "daily_loss_limit_pct": -0.05,
    "daily_loss_limit_note": "intraday NAV drawdown <= -5% -> HALT: Mafee stops new orders + cancels pending, Spyros confirms via BOT_STOP. Chosen [REDACTED]22 (user); V2.4 backtest MaxDD ~ -19% so -5%/day is a disaster brake, not a normal-red-day trip.",
    "plan_deviation_tolerance_pct": 0.05,
    "plan_deviation_note": "if live fill vs approved plan deviates > 5% (qty or value), Mafee STOPS and reports (append_event Mafee error) instead of improvising."
  },
  "macro_kill_switches": {
    "_principle": "Three macro/episode-level suspends on the RECOVERY_PARK (deep-cheap deploy) sleeve, required by Spyros's v24-golive-risk-review sign-off ([REDACTED]23) before go-live [REDACTED]30. These are SLOWER, regime-level brakes — distinct from the intraday execution brakes in risk_circuit_breakers. Each SUSPENDS new recovery deploy when its trigger arms (auto-disarms when the trigger clears — 'suspend', not permanent off), EXCEPT the drawdown breaker (C) which HALTS via BOT_STOP and requires human review to restart. They do NOT touch the static core book (BAL/LAG); they gate only the opportunistic recovery sleeve and any >1.0x lever portion. Owners: Spyros enforces via risk_monitor.py + BOT_STOP; DollarBill must not plan new recovery adds while any switch is armed; Mafee hard-blocks recovery-sleeve orders while armed.",
    "A_sbv_rate_suspend": {
      "trigger": "SBV deposit rate (Big-4 12M term, causal/announced) > 0.075 (7.5%)",
      "source": "deposit_rate_vn.DEPOSIT_EVENTS; live figure confirmed via data/macro_health.json (Winston/Mafee). Freshness-gated: if the deposit feed is stale, fail SAFE (treat as armed -> no new recovery deploy).",
      "action": "SUSPEND — no NEW RECOVERY_PARK deploy and no NEW >1.0x lever while armed. Existing positions held (not force-unwound). Auto-disarms when deposit rate falls back <= 7.5%.",
      "rationale": "Outer hard-stop layer ON TOP of the existing deep_cheap_recovery_override.money_condition throttle (which already linearly scales deploy to 0 between deposit 7.5%->12%). At deposit >7.5% cash earns >=7.5% risk-free AND high-rate crises are historically L-shaped/slow (2012 SBV ~14% deep-cheap deploy LOST to baseline — backtest_recovery_alloc_2011.py). 7.5% = the dep_floor already pinned in money_condition; this switch is the discrete debounced suspend on top of the continuous throttle. DORMANT since 2014 (SBV <=6% throughout) — forward insurance for a future rate spike."
    },
    "B_valuation_richening_suspend": {
      "trigger": "median liquid-universe pb_z > -0.3 WHILE a RECOVERY episode is active",
      "source": "median PB z-score across data/ticker_prune liquid universe vs each name's own 5Y history, causal (T-1). Same pb_z series that gates deep_cheap_recovery_override episode-open (<= -0.5) and the lever portion (<= -0.7).",
      "action": "TIGHTEN — stop ADDING to the recovery sleeve (no new deploy); hold existing recovery positions. Auto-disarms (re-allows adds) only if pb_z falls back <= -0.5 (episode-open level).",
      "rationale": "The recovery thesis is 'deploy WHILE genuinely cheap'. Episode opens at pb_z <= -0.5; once the universe richens back above -0.3 the cheapness edge is gone and continuing to deploy is chasing a no-longer-cheap tape. The -0.5-in / -0.3-out asymmetric band is deliberate HYSTERESIS to avoid whipsaw around a single threshold. This is a sizing tightener, not a halt — it does not write BOT_STOP."
    },
    "C_episode_drawdown_breaker": {
      "trigger": "cumulative NAV drawdown since the recovery episode's entry point > -0.15 (-15%)",
      "threshold_note": "UPDATED -12% -> -15% ([REDACTED]27) per mge20-tail-review: ceiling raised to MGE=1.5x, so the wider position warrants 3pp more tolerance before S4 fires. At 1.5x the tail distribution allows slightly deeper transient loss before a genuine knife-catch. -12% was calibrated for 1.3x (tighter position, tighter brake).",
      "source": "NAV tracked from data/eod_account_<date>.json since the episode entry date (first deploy of the active recovery episode); Spyros risk_monitor.py persists episode state at data/recovery_episode_state.json. This is a CUMULATIVE episode drawdown, NOT the intraday measure.",
      "action": "HALT — write data/BOT_STOP (forced unwind / knife-catching circuit breaker): Mafee stops new orders + cancels pending, Spyros confirms. NO auto-restart — requires human review; manual override window 24h. If firing within 6 months of go-live ([REDACTED] to 2026-12-31) Spyros flags halt-review on bus.",
      "rationale": "Distinct from risk_circuit_breakers.daily_loss_limit_pct (-5% intraday disaster brake). This is the SLOW knife-catcher: if the book has bled -15% from where the recovery deploy started, the deep-cheap thesis for THIS episode is failing (still falling) — cut rather than average deeper into a falling knife.",
      "implement_note": "BOT_STOP file + Telegram alert + bus decision event. Manual override within 24h; no automatic restart without documented human review (Spyros + user). Episode state in data/recovery_episode_state.json; opened auto when lever fire detected, closed on S4 or manual --close-episode."
    },
    "_cross_ref": {
      "vs_risk_circuit_breakers": "risk_circuit_breakers = fast intraday execution brakes (-5%/day, plan-deviation). macro_kill_switches = slow regime/episode-level suspends on the recovery sleeve. Both can write BOT_STOP; (C) here is the only macro one that halts.",
      "vs_deep_cheap_recovery_override": "These switches GATE that override: (A) duplicates the money_condition floor as a discrete suspend; (B) is the exit-side of the pb_z episode band (override opens at -0.5, B suspends adds above -0.3); (C) bounds the override's downside per episode. The override remains status PROPOSED/paper until user go-live approval.",
      "status": "PROPOSED — paper. Spec authored by [REDACTED]risk), wired by Taylor. applies_to stays 'paper' and approved_by stays null until user explicitly approves live."
    }
  },
  "v25_leverage": {
    "_principle": "V2.5 = V2.4 + leverage (user naming [REDACTED]27). The ONLY difference vs V2.4 (leverage-free, go-live [REDACTED]30) is the deep-cheap recovery LEVER. This block documents the V2.5-specific account + broker + gates; the sizing/MGE/breaker policy already lives in execution_limits.deep_cheap_recovery_override + macro_kill_switches. STATUS=[REDACTED] until live-recommend integration + final user go-ahead (post-go-live).",
    "status": "[REDACTED] (prep). Paper until: (1) live-recommend integration of the lever signals, (2) explicit user live go-ahead. Go-live [REDACTED]30 = V2.4 leverage-free; V2.5 does NOT affect it.",
    "config": "state-blind + PE-pctile gate recovery-LEVER, MGE 1.50 (Spyros-approved; MGE_HARD 1.65), deploy vehicle = yieldcombo (pbcombo rejected — worse risk-adjusted), entry = A∧C-confirm capitulation + pb_z<=-0.5 + PE_pctile5y<=0.20.",
    "account": {
      "subaccount": "[REDACTED]",
      "loan_package_id": 1840,
      "package_name": "[REDACTED]",
      "borrow_rate_annual": 0.125,
      "initial_rate": 0.5,
      "maintenance_rate": 0.4,
      "liquid_rate": 0.3,
      "collateral": "all 28 [REDACTED]V tickers eligible (Mafee DNSE probe [REDACTED]27)",
      "user_confirmed": "[REDACTED]27",
      "note": "DNSE call at maintenance 0.4 = -44.4% PORTFOLIO drop (= -66.7% NAV at 1.5x); force-sell at liquid 0.3 = -52.4% portfolio. Borrow 12.5% (not the backtest 10%) — re-verified: lever net edge SURVIVES (+1.00pp vs leverage-free, ~identical to 10%; carry trivial as lever borrows little+briefly)."
    },
    "safety_gates": {
      "B2_episode_breaker": "Spyros risk_monitor.py: -15% NAV from episode-entry -> BOT_STOP (macro_kill_switches.C_episode_drawdown_breaker). DONE.",
      "B3_nav_cap": "lever auto-[REDACTED] above NAV 100B (capacity-bound >~100B per #10). Engine lever_nav_cap (prior-session NAV check per lever-date), pt_v23 LEVER_NAV_CAP_B=100. DONE+verified (@150B gross 1.0).",
      "B4_pe_freshness": "state-blind lever requires fresh VNINDEX_PE (prior-month present AND feed <=2 months stale); else fail-closed to leverage-free. DONE.",
